.TH RADIOSTYX 1
.SH NAME
radiostyx \- Styx over the radio, and the message size it settles on
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B radiostyx
.B serve
.RB [ ssl ]
.br
.B radiostyx
.B get
.RI [ path
.RB [ ssl ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Serve
exports the namespace over
.BR /dev/radio0/data .
.B Get
walks to
.I path
on the other end, reads it and prints it, first printing the message
size the two agreed on.  With
.B ssl
as a last argument both push
.IR ssl (3)
onto the radio first.
.PP
It exists to run the argument in
.B doc/pycubed-plan.ms
that a satellite needs no change to speak Styx over a radio-sized
message, because
.B exportfs
adopts the transport's
.B iounit
when negotiating \-
.B os/inferno/port/exportfs.c:806
turns an iounit above 64 and below the requested size into the size.
.PP
The ground half does not use
.IR mount (2),
on purpose.
.B os/inferno/port/devmnt.c:195
refuses a message size below 256 and a radio payload is 251, which is
the argument's whole point: the floor is on the client, and the client
is a workstation.
.B appl/lib/styx.b
has no floor, so this speaks Styx directly.
.SH EXAMPLE
On the satellite,
.B "radiostyx serve" ;
on the ground,
.BR "radiostyx get dev/battery" .
The ground asks for 8192 and prints what it got:
.IP
.EX
RADIOSTYX-MSIZE 251 version 9P2000
RADIOSTYX-READ '3960
'
.EE
.PP
251 is the radio's payload budget, arrived at by the server without
being told.
.SH BUGS
The message size is not adopted through
.IR ssl (3).
.B exportfs
reads the iounit of the file it was handed, and with
.I ssl
pushed on, that is the
.I ssl
device's and not the radio's, so the same exchange settles on 8192:
.IP
.EX
RADIOSTYX-SSL #D/0
RADIOSTYX-MSIZE 8192 version 9P2000
.EE
.PP
The reads above still worked, because what came back was about 210
bytes against a 251-byte budget \- it fitted by luck and not by
arrangement.  A reply over the budget would be refused by the radio,
with the error naming the budget.  Over
.I ssl
the ground has to ask for a size the link can carry, which it can,
having no floor; it is the automatic part that is missing.
.PP
The client is one exchange deep: one walk, one open, one read, no
clunk, and no second read for a file longer than one reply.  It is a
demonstration of the transport, not a file system client.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/radiostyx.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR radio (3),
.IR radiossl (1),
.IR styx (2)
